Rescue Recipes section on /recipes

Bring back a "Perfect Match"-style card section on /recipes, but scoped to expiring pantry items (rescue), and deep-linkable from the Pantry rescue alert's "Recipe" button.

Behavior





Only render the section when rescueItems.length > 0. If no items are expiring, the section is hidden entirely.



Section title: "Cook before it expires" (FR: "À cuisiner avant péremption"), with a subline naming the focused expiring item(s).



Use the existing matched recipes from the match-recipes query (already passes expiringItems). Filter to recipes whose ingredients include at least one rescue item (via the existing filterRecipesForRescue helper in src/lib/rescueFilter.ts).



If the URL has ?rescue=true&item=<name> (as dispatched by RescueAlerts on /pantry), narrow the filter to that specific item; the chosen item is shown as a chip at the top of the section.



Show up to 3 recipe cards using the same RecipeCard styling already used elsewhere on the page (favorite, cook now, add-to-grocery actions all wired to existing handlers).



Loading state: 2 RecipeCardSkeletons while matchLoading.



Empty state (rescue items exist but no matches yet): small note "We're finding recipes for {item}…" plus a "Generate one for me" button that triggers the existing AI generation flow with focusIngredient = item.

Deep-link / scroll





On mount (and whenever location.search changes), if ?rescue=true is present, scroll the section into view smoothly (scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "start" })) after the first matched recipes paint. Use a useRef<HTMLDivElement> on the section wrapper and a useEffect keyed on [location.search, matchLoading].



The RescueAlerts "Recipe" button already navigates with the correct params — no changes needed in src/components/RescueAlerts.tsx.

Placement in src/pages/RecipesMerged.tsx

Insert directly after the "expiring warning" block (currently lines 1363–1389) and before the "Create a recipe just for you" custom-recipe hub (currently starting at line 1392). The section reuses existing state: rescueItems, matched, matchLoading, pantryItems, plus the existing card handlers (handleCookNow, toggleFavorite, addToGroceryList, expand/collapse).

Technical details





Read query params with new URLSearchParams(location.search) (no new dep). Extract rescueParam = sp.get("rescue") === "true" and focusItem = sp.get("item").



Filter:

const rescueRecipes = useMemo(() => {
  if (!matched || rescueItems.length === 0) return [];
  return filterRecipesForRescue(matched, focusItem)
    .filter((r) =>
      (r.ingredients_json || []).some((ing) =>
        rescueItems.some((ri) =>
          ing.name?.toLowerCase().includes(ri.item_name.toLowerCase()) ||
          ri.item_name.toLowerCase().includes(ing.name?.toLowerCase() ?? "")
        )
      )
    )
    .slice(0, 3);
}, [matched, rescueItems, focusItem]);



Section JSX is gated by rescueItems.length > 0. Inside, gate the cards list by rescueRecipes.length > 0, otherwise show the empty/generate state.

